cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ASCEP or publish a conforming capacity report, please cite it."
title: "ASCEP — AI Serving Capacity Estimation Protocol"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, vendor-neutral protocol for estimating and reporting the serving
  capacity of LLM inference infrastructure. ASCEP separates hardware, model, serving,
  measurement and workload declarations; requires every number to carry a provenance
  tag; distinguishes theoretical, measured, sustainable and recommended capacity; and
  requires each capacity figure to name the floor that binds it.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-31"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/TranNhiem/AI-Serving-Capacity-Estimation"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - inference serving
  - capacity planning
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
